{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/pulls/1047","id":4947602525,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSDCHbc8AAAABJuZsXQ","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify/pull/1047","diff_url":"https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify/pull/1047.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify/pull/1047.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/issues/1047","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/pulls/1047/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/pulls/1047/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/issues/1047/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/statuses/82faee7567769f6496315ae289ee331e4dd22849","number":1047,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(story): exclude flowless guides from the opening clock","user":{"login":"tt-a1i","id":53142663,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTQyNjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53142663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-a1i","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-a1i/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem and value\n\nFlowless guides were counted as Story opening events. On the bundled waterfall, their synthetic travel stretched the opening from the node horizon of 1.9 seconds to 3.2589 seconds; a longer guide could speed up the establish shot unnecessarily.\n\nThe opening clock now counts only edges with an actual native transfer. Flowless guides retain their fallback travel when a later scene traces them, and real transfers still extend the opening. This is a Story timing correction; authored diagram geometry is unchanged.\n\n## Integration and scope\n\n#1036 has already merged. Its ranged-audio correction and current dev's newer FFmpeg diagnostics remain in the base. This PR now contains only the remaining opening-clock fix, its browser regression, and the canonical archive.\n\nFinal head `a1433505d2f67c59fc9a587dfe409d9ad7a9d188` preserves contributor head `b29fa4ae8e6ec411d1e4bb1309b2adef5ddd45d6` and merges dev `82c7e0f089a02a4d514714adf37dc2061682da5f`. Relative to dev: three source-line additions/two removals in `archify/story/story.js`, 37 browser-test lines, and `archify.zip`. The archive's only changed entry is `archify/story/story.js`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Current-dev control fails the existing focused browser regression: waterfall opening span 3.258903394426618 versus node horizon 1.9. The candidate passes, including the extended flowless guide and real-transfer workflow controls.\n- Final source: Story browser, Story node and release-package checks — 60 passed, 2 platform skips, 0 failed. Real Chrome and FFmpeg 9.0.2/ffprobe were configured; existing early/late ranged-video audio decode checks executed.\n- `npm run test:generated` and `git diff --check` passed. Official Node 22.23.3 / zlib 1.3.1-e00f703 produced the archive. Viewer/gallery/example inputs are unchanged, so their outputs required no additional refresh.\n- Hosted CI must be assessed on this published final head. Local runtime assertions establish timing and decode behavior; they are not a new human visual sign-off.\n\nThe scoped improvement check found no additional abstraction or test expansion worthwhile inside this timing correction.\n\n## AI assistance and accountability\n\nOriginal follow-up: Cursor Grok 4.7, accountable contributor @tt-a1i, retaining the #1036 contributor history. Maintainer update: Codex (`gpt-6.1-sol`) reviewed the current scope, integrated dev, verified the regression and real decoder, regenerated the archive, and updated this description.\n\n- [ ] I reviewed the submitted changes and explanation, understand their impact, and can answer questions about them. Validation results and gaps are recorded above.\n\n## Apache-base integration (2026-10-25)\n\nNormal merge of frozen dev `3f95f0349c8276db71509ca239461b6fe9d00f9f`; candidate `82faee7567769f6496315ae289ee331e4dd22849`. Retains original contributor history, the scoped opening-clock fix and current Apache/historical-MIT/NOTICE/third-party notice files. Only ZIP conflicted and was rebuilt from the combined tracked source.\n\nOfficial Node 22.23.3: focused real-Chrome flowless-opening regression 1 pass / 0 fail / 0 skip; Story unit/public-CLI suite 21 pass / 0 fail / 0 skip; standalone software-notice regression passed. Independent Story attachment probe verifies exact notice text in both the outer retained native HTML and the embedded Story HTML. Canonical ZIP double build is byte-identical; extracted package notice files match source and package smoke passes without dependencies.\n\nPrior actual FFmpeg 9.0.2/ffprobe ranged-audio decode evidence at a1433505 is reused at its original identity: Story timing/audio/export/webm source files are byte-identical, while this merge's Story tool addition is nonvisual notice data. No new decoder result or human visual sign-off is claimed. Current opening/attachment behavior was checked on this candidate. Final CI remains required on the combined integration revision. No release or live installation.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T06:51:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T09:19:31Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T09:19:31